// Phase 11.7.a — reactive interpolated child props (`.fitzv` → WASM).
//
// The first client-WASM slice of Phase 11.7 (client-side dynamic
// capabilities). A parent `App` passes two of its OWN state fields
// down to a `<Badge />` child as INTERPOLATED props:
//
//   <Badge heading="{title}" count="{clicks + 1}" />
//
// Under the dirty-flag reactivity model, clicking the parent's
// "bump" button mutates `clicks`, which re-renders `App`, which
// recomputes the child's props and re-mounts it — so `count`
// tracks the parent's state live. Reactive propagation falls out
// of the naive re-render for free; no signals, no VDOM.
//
// Contract of shape (Phase 11.7.a subset):
//   - Interpolated props target a PRIMITIVE child field
//     (`Int`/`Float`/`Str`/`Bool`).
//   - The prop expression is a bare parent state field (`{title}`)
//     or numeric arithmetic over parent state (`{clicks + 1}`).
//   - Event bodies stay numeric (assigning a `Str` to state is a
//     separate 11.4.c debt), so `title` is constant here — it
//     still exercises the interpolated Str-prop emit path.
//
// PERSISTENT CHILD STATE (Phase 11.7.e, R2 v0.21.6) — the parent
// caches each `<Child />` instance in a typed slot, so a child is
// REUSED (not recreated) across parent re-renders. That means a
// child can hold its own local state and keep it: `Badge` below has
// a `taps` counter with its own `@click` — click the badge a few
// times, then click "bump the parent"; the parent re-renders (the
// `count` prop updates) but the badge's `taps` survives, because the
// same cached `Badge` instance is re-mounted. Before 11.7.e (R1) the
// child was recreated on every parent re-render and `taps` reset.

component App {
  state {
    title: Str = "Fitz reactive props"
    clicks: Int = 0
  }

  event bump() { clicks = clicks + 1 }

  <template>
    <div class="app">
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="hint">Click below — the parent's <code>clicks</code> flows into the child's <code>count</code> prop.</p>
      <button class="bump" @click="bump">bump the parent</button>
      <Badge heading="{title}" count="{clicks + 1}" />
    </div>
  </template>

  <style scoped>
    .app { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
    .hint { color: #666; font-size: 0.9em; }
    .bump { padding: 8px 16px; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 6px; background: white; }
  </style>
}

component Badge {
  state {
    heading: Str = ""
    count: Int = 0
    taps: Int = 0
  }

  event tap() { taps = taps + 1 }

  <template>
    <div class="badge">
      <div class="heading">{heading}</div>
      <div class="count">parent bumps + 1 = {count}</div>
      <button class="tap" @click="tap">my own taps: {taps}</button>
    </div>
  </template>

  <style scoped>
    .badge { border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; margin-top: 16px; background: #fafafa; }
    .heading { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #666; }
    .count { font-size: 1.6em; font-weight: bold; margin: 8px 0; }
    .tap { padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 6px; background: white; }
  </style>
}
